Menu="Utilities"
Title="WebUI Links"
Icon="external-link"
Tag="external-link"
---
<?php
$webuiLinksPlugin = 'webui-links';
require_once "$docroot/plugins/$webuiLinksPlugin/include/links.php";
$webuiLinksCfg = webui_links_cfg();
$webuiLinksMap = webui_links_map($webuiLinksCfg['NPM_CONF_DIR'] ?? '');
?>
<form markdown="1" method="POST" action="/update.php" target="progressFrame">
<input type="hidden" name="#file" value="webui-links/webui-links.cfg">

_(Enable)_:
: <select name="ENABLED">
  <?=mk_option($webuiLinksCfg['ENABLED'] ?? 'yes', 'yes', _('Yes'))?>
  <?=mk_option($webuiLinksCfg['ENABLED'] ?? 'yes', 'no', _('No'))?>
  </select>

:webui_links_enable_plug:
> When enabled, a container's **WebUI** menu entry opens its Nginx Proxy Manager domain,
> and a second entry opens the direct IP:port address.
:end

_(NPM proxy host folder)_:
: <input type="text" name="NPM_CONF_DIR" class="wide" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($webuiLinksCfg['NPM_CONF_DIR'] ?? '')?>">

:webui_links_dir_plug:
> Folder holding Nginx Proxy Manager's proxy host files (`data/nginx/proxy_host` inside its appdata).
> The files are only read, never changed.
:end

_(Direct entry label)_:
: <input type="text" name="DIRECT_LABEL" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($webuiLinksCfg['DIRECT_LABEL'] ?? '')?>">

:webui_links_label_plug:
> Text of the second menu entry. `{address}` is replaced with the container's IP:port.
:end

&nbsp;
: <input type="submit" name="#apply" value="_(Apply)_"><input type="button" value="_(Done)_" onclick="done()">
</form>

<div class="title"><span class="left"><i class="fa fa-sitemap title"></i>_(Proxy hosts found)_</span></div>

<?if (!$webuiLinksMap):?>
<p>_(No proxy hosts found in that folder.)_</p>
<?else:?>
<table class="unraid tablesorter">
<thead><tr><th>_(Direct address)_</th><th>_(WebUI opens)_</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<?foreach ($webuiLinksMap as $address => $url):?>
<tr><td><?=htmlspecialchars($address)?></td><td><?=htmlspecialchars($url)?></td></tr>
<?endforeach;?>
</tbody>
</table>
<?endif;?>
